//==============================================================================
// add_pad : power / ground pads of mcu_pad_top (48-pad ring, 12 pads per side)
//   Included by mcu_pad_top.v at the end of the module (`include "add_pad").
//   Everything is commented out for now. When the power pads are needed
//   (PnR), remove the "//" marks. These cells have no signal ports.
//
//   Pad cells : PADVDD    core power        PADVSS    core ground
//               PADVDDIOR I/O ring power    PADVSSIOR I/O ring ground
//
//   Ring order (numbers follow the ring, counter-clockwise from the left side):
//     Left   : pad1  ~ pad12    Bottom : pad13 ~ pad24
//     Right  : pad25 ~ pad36    Top    : pad37 ~ pad48
//   Every side has the same pattern (position 1..12):
//     1 VSSIOR | 2 3 4 signal | 5 VDD | 6 VSS | 7 8 9 10 11 signal | 12 VDDIOR
//   The signal slots (positions 2,3,4,7,8,9,10,11) are in mcu_pad_top.v.
//   Total : 16 power pads + 32 signal slots (15 used, 17 reserved) = 48 pads.
//   If more power pads are needed, a reserved signal slot can be used for one.
//==============================================================================

